      `the application is made without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 67 r 2(1)(a) an application for a warrant for search and seizure under section 11(1)(a)` THEN
        IF `the application is made without notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be made without notice"; the Rule does not say what follows
    WHEN `o 67 r 2(1)(b) an application for a restraint order under section 11(1)(b)` THEN
        IF `the application is made without notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be made without notice"; the Rule does not say what follows
    WHEN `o 67 r 2(1) another application` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application for (a) a warrant ... or (b) a restraint order"

