         WHEN `o 67 r 6(2) security given by the Public Trustee` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not necessary ... for the Public Trustee to give security"
         WHEN `o 67 r 6 another requirement of Order 13, Rule 9` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks only of the affidavit of fitness and security

@ref O 67 r 6(1) (src:7626)
GIVEN `the Public Trustee is appointed under section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      requirement IS A `o 67 r 6 requirement of Order 13, Rule 9`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 6(1) the requirement of Order 13, Rule 9 applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Public Trustee is appointed under section 15`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Order 13, Rule 9 applies where the Public Trustee is appointed under section 15"
    ELSE IF `o 67 r 6(2) the requirement is necessary` `the Public Trustee is appointed under section 15` requirement EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

