-- src:7628 | 7. —(1) An application by a person appointed under section 15 for a destruction order under section 16(2) must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit which must — ( a )
-- src:7629 | state the full particulars of the property to be destroyed; and
-- src:7630 | ( b )
-- src:7631 | state the reasons for destroying the property.
@ref O 67 r 7(1) (src:7628-7631)
GIVEN `the application is by a person appointed under section 15 for a destruction order under section 16(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the full particulars of the property to be destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the reasons for destroying the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 7(1) the application is filed and served with the affidavit the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is by a person appointed under section 15 for a destruction order under section 16(2)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application by a person appointed under section 15 for a destruction order under section 16(2)"
    ELSE IF    `the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit`
           AND `the affidavit states the full particulars of the property to be destroyed`
           AND `the affidavit states the reasons for destroying the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit"; the Rule does not say what follows

-- src:7632 | (2) The application and the supporting affidavit must be served on — ( a )
-- src:7633 | the Public Prosecutor; and
-- src:7634 | ( b )
-- src:7635 | any person having a valid interest in the property to be destroyed,
-- src:7636 | within 14 days after the date of filing of the application.
@ref O 67 r 7(2) (src:7632-7636)
`o 67 r 7(2) the period for serving` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 67 r 7(2) (src:7632-7636)
GIVEN `the application is one to which paragraph (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person having a valid interest in the property to be destroyed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 7(2) the application and affidavit are served within the period` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is one to which paragraph (1) applies`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The application" is the one in paragraph (1)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person having a valid interest in the property to be destroyed`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): not yet served on everyone; the 14 days may still be running
         WHEN JUST done THEN
             IF done AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of filing of the application"

