-- src:7638 | 8. —(1) An application for an order of forfeiture under section 21 must be entitled in the matter of the owner or person who has control of the property, if known, naming that owner or person as the defendant, and in the matter of the Act, and all subsequent documents in the matter must be so entitled. (2) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit which must — ( a )
@ref O 67 r 8(1) (src:7638)
GIVEN `the application is for an order of forfeiture under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or person who has control of the property is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is entitled in the matter of the owner or person who has control of the property, naming that owner or person as the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 8(1) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is for an order of forfeiture under section 21`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application for an order of forfeiture under section 21"
    ELSE IF    (    (NOT (`the owner or person who has control of the property is known`))
                 OR `the application is entitled in the matter of the owner or person who has control of the property, naming that owner or person as the defendant`)
           AND `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act`
           AND `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be entitled"; the Rule does not say what follows

-- src:7638 | 8. —(1) An application for an order of forfeiture under section 21 must be entitled in the matter of the owner or person who has control of the property, if known, naming that owner or person as the defendant, and in the matter of the Act, and all subsequent documents in the matter must be so entitled. (2) The application must be filed and served with a supporting affidavit which must — ( a )
