-- src:7661 | 10. Despite Order 26, Rule 3, no person may inspect or take a copy of any document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge.
@ref O 67 r 10 (src:7661)
GIVEN `the document was filed under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission of a Judge has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 1 r 3(1) the person who gave permission is a Judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document was filed under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document filed under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the permission of a Judge has been given` AND `o 1 r 3(1) the person who gave permission is a Judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the permission of a Judge" lifts the bar and grants nothing (QA); Order 26, Rule 3 is untouched
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person may inspect or take a copy of any document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge"

@ref O 67 r 10 (src:7661)
GIVEN `the document was filed under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission of a Judge has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 1 r 3(1) the person who gave permission is a Judge` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the document was filed under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document filed under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the permission of a Judge has been given` AND `o 1 r 3(1) the person who gave permission is a Judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is lifted by the permission of a Judge
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 67 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names the Public Prosecutor or the applicant as the actor.  Where the text gives 14 days the rule below carries a WITHIN of 14 days after filing; the day count (clear days, non-court days) is Order 3, Rule 3's and is not repeated, so the rules count in days.

DECLARE `o 67 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 67 the applicant`
    `o 67 the Public Prosecutor`
    `o 67 any person`

DECLARE `o 67 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit`
    `o 67 serve copies of the restraint order`
    `o 67 inspect or take a copy of a document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge`

-- src:7605 | 3. —(1) An application by the Public Prosecutor under section 18 to revoke or vary a warrant or an order made under Part IV of the Act must be made by summons. (2) The application to revoke or vary a warrant issued under section 11(1)( a ) or an order issued under section 11(1)( b ) and an affidavit in support thereof must be filed and served on — ( a )
-- src:7606 | any person having any interest in the property to which the application relates; and
-- src:7607 | ( b )
-- src:7608 | any person appointed under section 15(1),
-- src:7609 | within 14 days after the date of filing of the application.
@ref O 67 r 3(2) (src:7605-7609)
`o 67 r 3(2) the Public Prosecutor's duty to file and serve` MEANS
    PARTY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor`
    MUST `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor` BECAUSE "the application to revoke or vary and the affidavit were not filed and served within 14 days after the date of filing"

-- src:7632 | (2) The application and the supporting affidavit must be served on — ( a )
-- src:7633 | the Public Prosecutor; and
-- src:7634 | ( b )
-- src:7635 | any person having a valid interest in the property to be destroyed,
-- src:7636 | within 14 days after the date of filing of the application.
@ref O 67 r 7(2) (src:7632-7636)
`o 67 r 7(2) the applicant's duty to serve` MEANS
    PARTY `o 67 the applicant`
    MUST `o 67 file and serve the application and affidavit`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 67 the applicant` BECAUSE "the application for a destruction order and the supporting affidavit were not served within 14 days after the date of filing"

-- src:7600 | (6) Where a restraint order is issued under section 11(1)( b ), the Public Prosecutor must — ( a )
-- src:7601 | unless the Court otherwise provides, serve copies of the order and supporting affidavit on the defendant and, where property to which the order relates is held by another person, on that person; and
-- src:7602 | ( b )
-- src:7603 | serve a copy of the order on all other persons affected by the order.
@ref O 67 r 2(6) (src:7600-7603)
`o 67 r 2(6) the Public Prosecutor's duty to serve the restraint order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor`
    MUST `o 67 serve copies of the restraint order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 67 the Public Prosecutor` BECAUSE "copies of the restraint order were not served as the Rule requires"

-- src:7661 | 10. Despite Order 26, Rule 3, no person may inspect or take a copy of any document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge.
@ref O 67 r 10 (src:7661)
`o 67 r 10 the prohibition on inspecting a document filed under this Order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 67 any person`
    SHANT `o 67 inspect or take a copy of a document filed under this Order without the permission of a Judge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 67 any person` BECAUSE "a document filed under this Order was inspected or copied without the permission of a Judge"
